   286	
   287	
   288	
   289	**(a) CVE-2017-1000498 [28]**
   290	
   291	
   292	**(b) CVE-2016-8739 [27]**
   293	
   294	
   295	**(c) CVE-2018-11797 [30]**
   296	
   297	
   298	**Figure 1: Examples of “semantic redundancy”:** _**diff**_ **lines ex-**
   299	**cerpted from full security patches.**
   300	
   301	
   302	leading spaces/tabs, these lines would be identical. In other words,
   303	the actual semantic-related change of the patch is the try-catch
   304	environment, rather than these four statements. Similar cases include moving statements into if-else, for, or while blocks. In
   305	the second case (Figure 1b), lines 1 and 3 differ due to the change
   306	of a variable (i.e., is −→ reader ). The change originates from
   307	calling the method createXMLStreamReader . Thus, the code that
