     1	# PPT4J
     2	
     3	[![DOI](https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.10397354.svg)](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10397354)
     4	[![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker%20Hub-zhiyuanpan/ppt4j-blue.svg)](https://hub.docker.com/r/zhiyuanpan/ppt4j)
     5	
     6	
     7	This is the replication package for the ICSE 2024 paper *"PPT4J: Patch Presence Test for Java Binaries"*.
     8	
     9	**Note:** For more details on the paper, please refer to [https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3597503.3639231](https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3597503.3639231).
    10	
    11	**Note:** The documentation page is now available at [https://pan2013e.github.io/ppt4j](https://pan2013e.github.io/ppt4j).
    12	
    13	---
    14	
    15	## Project structure
    16	
    17	```
    18	.
    19	├── Dockerfile
    20	├── README.md
    21	├── all.iml
    22	├── download.sh
    23	├── framework
    24	├── lib
    25	├── misc
    26	├── pom.xml
    27	├── replicate_rq1.py
    28	├── scripts
    29	└── urls.txt
    30	```
    31	
    32	- The `framework` folder contains the code of PPT4J
    33	- The `misc` folder contains an example of using PPT4J
    34	  - Please checkout `misc/src/main/java/ppt4j/Demo.java` for detailed usage.
    35	- The `scripts` folder contains utility scripts, written in Python
    36	- The `lib` folder contains necessary jars
    37	
    38	## Requirements
    39	
    40	Note: We provide Docker images for replication. If you use Docker, you can just jump to the section "Using docker".
    41	
    42	### System requirements
    43	
    44	- This project is a prototype implementation and only supports UNIX-like operating systems.
    45	
    46	### Software requirements
    47	
    48	- **JDK, Maven, Python**
    49	- The versions of software we use:
    50	  - JDK 17.0.2 (Java SE 17.0.2, Oracle HotSpot 64-Bit Server VM, build 17.0.2+8-LTS-86)
    51	  - Apache Maven 3.9.1
    52	  - Python 3.9.10
    53	- It should be fine if you use other recent versions of Maven and Python.
    54	- We strongly recommend that you use the same Oracle JDK 17.0.2 for replication. Run `export JAVA_HOME=...` command to make sure that maven uses the expected version of JDK.
    55	
    56	## Setting up the environment
    57	
    58	### On host machine
    59	
    60	- [Download the dataset](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10397354) and extract the items to your preferred location. Then set 
    61	  - `ppt4j.database.root` field in `framework/src/main/resources/ppt4j.properties` to that location. Or you can just extract to your home directory to make the property file unaltered.
    62	
    63	### Using Docker
    64	
    65	- We provide a [Docker image](https://hub.docker.com/r/zhiyuanpan/ppt4j) as an alternative. To start a container, the host system and architecture should be `Linux, x86_64(amd64)`.
    66	
    67	```bash
    68	# Host OS
    69	$ docker pull zhiyuanpan/ppt4j
    70	$ # alternative: docker pull zhiyuanpan/ppt4j:minimal-latest
    71	$ docker run --rm -it zhiyuanpan/ppt4j
    72	```
    73	
    74	- The docker images on Docker Hub have two tags: `minimal`(~250M download size, ~500M final usage) and `complete`(~13G download size, ~22G final usage). 
    75	  - The `complete` one provides an out-of-the-box experience (with dataset). Commands described in the next section can be executed without any further configuration.
    76	  - The `minimal` one provides a minimal running environment that satisfies software requirements (without dataset). To test the dataset in `minimal` containers, please first run `bash download.sh` in the **home directory**, and the script will start the downloading process. 
    77	- To test other Java binaries, you can mount custom directories in the `docker run` command.
    78	
    79	For detailed script/executable usage, please refer to the documentation below.
    80	
    81	## Run PPT4J
    82	
    83	For a quick start, you can run `python replicate_rq1.py` to get the results of RQ1 in the paper.
    84	
    85	You can also use the Python scripts inside the `scripts` folder for: **project building** and **testing**.
    86	
    87	- In the **project root** (where `README.md` and `all.iml` are located), run `python -m scripts.<name> <args>`.
    88	  - Available `<name>`: `build, test`
    89	  - `scripts.build`: wrapper of maven commands; no arg; build the `Java` projects
    90	  - `scripts.test`: perform tests on the dataset. Please leave `<args>` empty for detailed usage of this subcommand.
    91	- Example
    92	```bash
    93	$ python -m scripts.build
    94	$ python -m scripts.test postpatch 1
    95	
    96	[test.py           ]  INFO - Running test 1 postpatch
    97	[.a.p.PatchAnalyzer]  INFO - Ground truth binary type in dataset: postpatch
    98	[.a.p.PatchAnalyzer]  INFO - Analyzing patch for fastjson, CVE ID: CVE-2017-18349, Database ID: 1
    99	[.a.p.PatchAnalyzer]  INFO - Result: 1.0
   100	[p.u.AspectUtils   ]  INFO - Result: patch is present
   101	```
   102	
   103	```bash
   104	$ python -m scripts.test all
   105	```
   106	
   107	## Misc
   108	- The compiled PPT4J only works as separate bytecode files in `framework/target/classes`. Packing them into a jar and use the jar will lead to unexpected behaviours, due to our implementation and the classpath mechanism in newer Java versions.
   109	


